{"name":"Dustwallow Marsh","hex":"#685243","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marsh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of low, wet land, often with tall grass or herbaceous plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsh in shallow water on a lakeshore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoastal_marsh_profile.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White water lilies are a typical marsh plant in European areas of deeper wat